---
// Static footnotes explaining the coordinate system and controls.
---

<section class="model-notes">
  <h2>Notes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Units are Unreal centimeters (X forward, Y right, Z up); the scene is
      shown with Z-up.
    </li>
    <li>Drag to orbit, scroll to zoom, right-drag to pan.</li>
    <li>
      Parts cascade like the in-game hangar: a part's sockets (shoulders, weapon
      slots, gear) only appear once it is placed. Shoulders have zero, one or
      two weapon slots; titan torsos and shoulders are fixed by their chassis.
      Unreleased parts only appear when a link selects them.
    </li>
    <li>
      The URL always reflects the current build: one parameter per filled slot,
      named by where it mounts (e.g. <code>chassis</code>,
      <code>torso</code>, <code>Shoulder_L</code>,
      <code>Shoulder_L.Shoulder_Weapon_0</code>), plus <code>hitbox</code>. Copy
      the address bar to share an exact loadout.
    </li>
    <li>
      Weapon placement uses the build's socket chain plus the runtime mount
      rotation applied by the game (see docs/weapon_mount_findings.md).
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>

<style>
  .model-notes {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .model-notes ul {
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
  }
</style>
